title: "TCI Simulator: multi-model target-controlled infusion simulator with tolerance-of-laryngoscopy isoboles"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24058642
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vonRomans86/tci-simulator"
url: "https://vonromans86.github.io/tci-simulator/"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Romanelli
    given-names: Antonio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6895-6485"
    affiliation: "AOU San Giovanni di Dio e Ruggi d'Aragona, Salerno, Italy"
keywords:
  - anesthesia
  - target-controlled infusion
  - pharmacokinetics
  - pharmacodynamics
  - propofol
  - remifentanil
  - fentanyl
  - response surface
  - medical education
abstract: >-
  Browser-based target-controlled infusion (TCI) simulator for propofol,
  remifentanil, fentanyl, sufentanil and alfentanil, implementing the Eleveld,
  Schnider, Marsh, Paedfusor, Kataria, Minto, Shafer, Scott-Stanski, Gepts and
  Maitre models, with effect-site or plasma targeting, live
  tolerance-of-laryngoscopy isoboles (Bouillon 2004, Kern 2004), predicted BIS
  and CSV export at 0.5-s resolution. Teaching and simulation tool only, not
  for clinical use.
